WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.279
let's go to the phones on a very, very busy
news week.

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.460
(617) 830-4750.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.160
We will start with our caller from the three
one two area code.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.910
Let's go to our caller from the three one,
two.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.070
Hi David.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.430
This is Priscilla from Chicago.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.930
How are you?

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:21.930
Good.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.210
So the question just, I had a thought when
I was at the store.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.820
I see that you've major corporations, you
know, always ask before you pay.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:38.050
Um, you know, we were willing to donate two,
$3, um, to a good cause it ends up being a

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.550
good cause, but it just rubs me the wrong
way because it's like you're a multibillion

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.550
dollar corporation.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:49.219
Why don't you donate $1 billion to this corporation
instead of asking two or $3 from people who

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:52.950
are already maybe lower middle class, middle
class.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:57.050
And you know, when I talk about it to people,
their reaction seems to be kind of mixed.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:01.609
Like they're kind of torn because it is a
good cause like the children's hospital.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:07.890
But I don't get past the fact that these are
still billionaires asking for two, $3.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:12.540
Well, the big one is, um, I, I, I totally
agree with you and I am mixed in a sense because

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.470
I, I'm not saying that the cause isn't a good
one.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.790
I'm not saying that the issue of, you know,
childhood cancer is, is not an issue that

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:23.260
we should be taking seriously and, and working
to solve and you need money to solve that.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.340
Um, or hunger for example.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:30.500
But when I go to whole foods and you know,
that whole foods was, you know, trying to

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:35.040
prevent having to give employees healthcare
under Obamacare and all this different stuff,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.790
and then they're like, Hey, will you round
up your purchase or give us $1 or $5 for this

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:40.790
or that?

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.390
It's like, are you seriously asking me for
that given what you have been doing?

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:49.170
But at the same time, I don't want to suggest,
I don't care about the cause because I do,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.550
it is a really weird thing and I think it
works on guilt a lot.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.960
They want to guilt people into making these
donations.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.670
They use like, you know, a child's hospital,
which usually deals with like cancer and kids.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.150
And so you feel torn and you want to donate.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:07.210
But at the same time I feel angry because
it's already like you've taken so much and

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:12.629
I feel like the middle class, the poorest
people, you know, lower class, they shouldn't

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:18.849
be putting in more, you know, I feel like
it's a great cause then you put in more.

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:19.849
Absolutely.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:24.659
Now let me ask you, Priscilla, do you ever
do the donations?

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:29.769
You know, I used to, but I feel like as I
got older I think I got angrier.

00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:32.500
Like just got more cynical, I feel.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.260
Um, and I just, I felt like their care for
people as not really genuine.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:44.069
Um, so if I do do donations, I do directly
to the organizations versus going through

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:48.810
like, you know, whole foods or Walmart or
anyone who offers like that.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.209
That's exactly what I do and know.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:55.719
Part of it is when charities are a big uh,
area of scams.

00:02:55.719 --> 00:03:00.549
And I want to make sure that not only is the
money getting to the charity, but I want to

00:03:00.549 --> 00:03:05.889
make sure that the charity is also using the
money in a way that's responsible.

00:03:05.889 --> 00:03:09.989
So whenever I'm asked for any donation and
if it's at the grocery store, I just say,

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:10.989
no thank you.

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:15.310
But if I'm asked on the street or if someone
comes to the door soliciting, I always say,

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:22.620
listen, the way I decide is I proactively
seek out organizations that share my mission

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:26.400
and values and I make a contribution to them
after I've researched them.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.930
And those are my donations for the year.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.220
I don't like on a whim throw another five
or $10 at this or that thing.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.430
I think about, I put time into it and that's
what I do.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.730
That's it.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.560
And I feel like they've been doing it a lot
with like the hospitals now too.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:43.769
Like from my hospital, I am getting a lot
of like, Hey, donate, you know, $5 to this

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:49.090
good cause and it's you guys already charged
an arm and a leg to be seen there.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.030
And there's still, I mean

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:55.769
beyond that then you know, talking about donating
to hospitals, given the for profit private

00:03:55.769 --> 00:03:58.260
insurance system that we have, I mean it's
a mess.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.859
That's a, that's a complete other story for
a different day.

00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:01.950
But very good point.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.190
Priscilla, I appreciate you calling in and
making it.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.540
Thank you so much for taking my call.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.540
David.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.540
I'm a long time listener.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.540
Thank you.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.540
Hope to hear from you again.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:10.543
I appreciate it.

